    "exit_rule": "at least ten particles in the bowl and the container upright at the final state",
    "guidance": "**Measured scope/reliability:** Passed 9/12 (75%) fixed-protocol runs from its own demonstrated segment entry at action 180. Every run ended with all 12 particles in the bowl; the three failures ended tilted and still over the bowl. It was the second-best validated policy, but terminal righting remained the measured weakness.\n\n**Use when:** The grasp is secure and reachable and particle/source observations are reliable, especially when the current pour phase is ambiguous, discharge is unexpectedly early or late, or a modest local TCP correction is desired. The documents allow entry from early carry through tilt/righting within demonstrated relational phases, but validation directly measured only the action-180 entry.\n\n**Avoid/switch when:** There is a large global relocation for which local residuals may drift (h01 is the designated bowl-anchored alternative), an unusual but rigid grasp transform (h03 is designated), implausible/missing particle observations, oscillation between tilting and righting, grasp uncertainty, spill, collision, or non-converged IK. No unseen-error recovery was validated.\n\n**Recognize failure:** Enough particles alone is insufficient. The measured failures had all 12 particles transferred but `container_upright=false`. Also watch for tilt/righting oscillation, particles outside the bowl, changing source-to-TCP relation, or bad IK diagnostics.\n\n**Handoff:** Use observed physical evidence rather than the learned phase auxiliary: at least 10 particles settled, source approximately upright and securely held, and outbound motion begun. Hand off to `return_place_release` nominally near action 1680, within the supervised [1460,1740) overlap. The auxiliary phase prediction does not authorize handoff."
  },
